    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required deriving a `locality` field on the owner from its city, using the fixed table Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, returning the canonical region or `UNKNOWN` for unknown cities. The acceptance tests exercise this via `POST /api/owners` then `GET /api/owners/{id}` asserting `$.locality`.\n\nFollowing the project's existing Spring/OpenAPI conventions (the same pattern used for `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`, etc. \u2014 read-only derived fields declared in the OpenAPI spec and populated by the MapStruct mapper), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a fixed `CITY_REGION` table and a `formatLocality` method that returns `CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(owner.getCity(), \"UNKNOWN\")`.\n\nResults: `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) passes, and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (2 run, 0 failures).",
