    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe addition slots cleanly into the existing structure. `formatLocality` follows the exact same idiom as its siblings (`formatDisplayName`, `formatInitials`, `formatMembershipNumber`, `formatMembershipTier`): a `@Named` `default` derivation method with the null-owner guard, wired via a `@Mapping(..., qualifiedByName = ...)` entry on `toOwnerDto`. Logic lives in the right unit (DTO derivation belongs in the mapper), nothing is duplicated, the mapper is a natural home rather than a catch-all, and the `CITY_REGION` table is co-located immediately above its sole consumer. The OpenAPI `locality` field mirrors the neighbouring read-only derived fields. A maintainer of this file would find it entirely natural.\n\n(Minor, non-blocking nit only: `java.util.Map` is referenced by fully-qualified name while the file already imports `java.util.List`/`java.util.Collection`; an `import java.util.Map;` would match local style. Not a structural concern.)",
